        "id": 230325,
        "name": "catDreaming",
        "username": "catDreaming",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-04-20T04:36:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Not a synergy per se, but an efficient combo I stumbled onto.</p>\n<p>I've had success with Interceptor/Tank. Interceptor with Mark Target+Light Intercept is excellent at wearing down opposition when there are multiple foes, while Tank with Tackle can do the same in close range scenarios. Meanwhile, Interceptor can use Strafe Shot to wear down opposition over time while moving, while Tank can crush multiple foes at once with Inspiring Strike or use Challenge to grab attention (and armor up) with relative&nbsp;frequency.<br>\nPlus, both Strafe Shot and Inspiring Strike and Challenge all cost 2 AP, meaning that you can often change stance once during your turn if you need to take particular actions.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:05:17.658Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
